            "description": "THE AUTHORIZATION SERVER HAS NO PUBLIC ENDPOINT.\n\nVerified 2026-09-14: authz.dev.tripleq.ai does not resolve, and the Helm chart (deploy/helm/zonic-authz/templates/) contains no ingress template at all. Its only address is the in-cluster Service:\n\n    http://zonic-authorization-server.zonic-authz.svc.cluster.local\n\nThat is deliberate. Its only caller is the BFF, and it holds kms:Sign — putting an ALB in front of the component that mints tokens buys no routing benefit and widens the attack surface.\n\nTo exercise the endpoints listed in this folder, run from INSIDE the cluster (note curl is not in the image — use python3):\n\n    kubectl -n zonic-authz exec deploy/zonic-authz-token-provider -- python3 -c \\\n      \"import urllib.request as u; print(u.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/ready').read().decode())\"\n\nThis request itself just hits the BFF's /health so the folder is runnable; the value here is the documentation."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Discovery — GET /.well-known/openid-configuration (in-cluster)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authzInternalUrl}}/.well-known/openid-configuration",
              "host": [
                "{{authzInternalUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ".well-known",
                "openid-configuration"
              ]
            },
            "description": "In-cluster only. Advertises the issuer, the authorize/token/revoke endpoints and the JWKS location.\n\nThe issuer is http://zonic-authorization-server.zonic-authz.svc.cluster.local and it is a SIGNED CLAIM in every access token. Changing it — for example to give this service a public hostname — invalidates every token minted under the old value, so it is a coordinated change with the BFF, not a config tweak."
          }
